<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Proxymate.app (bundle.macOS.entitlements).

  Deliberately empty. Proxymate runs under the hardened runtime WITHOUT the
  App Sandbox (no com.apple.security.app-sandbox): the system proxy
  (networksetup), CA trust in the login keychain (SecTrustSettings), client
  app detection (libproc on other processes), the iOS Simulator and adb
  (spawning xcrun/adb) and the sysproxy guardian all need an unsandboxed
  process, and none of them needs a hardened-runtime exception:

  - No JIT or unsigned executable memory: WKWebView's JavaScript JIT runs
    in WebKit's own (Apple-signed) WebContent process, not ours.
  - No disable-library-validation: everything is statically linked; we
    load only system frameworks (and dlsym one libsystem symbol).
  - No allow-dyld-environment-variables, no get-task-allow (debugging;
    notarisation rejects it).
  - No automation.apple-events: we send no Apple Events to other apps.
  - Network client/server, files and keychain need no entitlement outside
    the sandbox.

  Add a key here only with a reason in docs/RELEASING.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
